    summary: ["Interview processes vary, but each round seeks a different kind of evidence.", "The job description should determine preparation emphasis and depth.", "A preparation matrix connects role requirements to current evidence and practice gaps.", "Strong answers lead with a direct response and add assumptions, trade-offs, and examples.", "Saying “I do not know” is professional when followed by a safe verification approach.", "Mock interviews are useful only when their observations change the next practice cycle.", "Two-, four-, and eight-week plans are sample planning frameworks, never readiness guarantees."],
