    summary: ["Production diagnosis begins with blast radius, timeline, versions, and preserved evidence.", "The first safe action contains harm without destroying the information needed to learn the cause.", "Offline success can fail online through leakage, skew, staleness, thresholds, or service defects.", "Model, preprocessing, feature, schema, policy, and runtime versions must move as a compatible bundle.", "Tail latency and batch deadlines require path-level traces, queue evidence, and capacity reasoning.", "Drift is a signal to investigate; it does not automatically prove model decay or justify deployment.", "A complete fix verifies recovery and adds a control that prevents the same failure from recurring."],
