    summary: ["A credible project story connects the problem, data, baseline, choices, evaluation, failure, result, and next step.", "Interviewers distinguish personal ownership from team contribution through detailed follow-up.", "Resume bullets should present defensible evidence rather than buzzwords or invented metrics.", "Measured impact needs a named baseline, metric, evaluation boundary, and honest scope.", "STAR becomes stronger when the action includes decision rationale, alternatives, and trade-offs.", "Failure, disagreement, ambiguity, incidents, and safety concerns reveal how you work under uncertainty.", "Frameworks organize genuine experience; they must never be used to fabricate a personal story."],
